1
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:49,484
Pass!

2
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:50,735
Hold up!

3
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:53,404
-Over here!
-I got it!

4
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,073
Got it!

5
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:57,659
Over here!

6
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:03,957
Over there!

7
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:09,254
{\an8}I’m basketball genius Hanamichi Sakuragi.

8
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:11,381
{\an8}Check out my superiority!

9
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:26,020
{\an8}<i>"Birth of a basketball genius?!"</i>

10
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:33,194
I'm sorry, Sakuragi-kun.

11
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,780
I like Oda-kun of the basketball team.

12
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:38,867
Shock!

13
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,035
{\an8}Congratulations, Hanamichi!

14
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:43,830
{\an8}Shot down by 50 girls in middle school!

15
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:46,541
{\an8}An unbreakable record!

16
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,500
You bunch of…

17
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:11,816
KANAGAWA PREFECTURE
SHOHOKU SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL

18
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,735
YEAR 1, CLASS 7

19
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:17,697
Hey, Yohei. How's Hanamichi holding up?

20
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,908
Still haven't gotten over it.

21
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,452
He's wallowing in his own self-pity.

22
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:25,413
I'd thought he'd get over it
in high school.

23
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:29,042
He's pretty introverted, you know…

24
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,877
even with his red hair.

25
00:03:32,128 --> 00:03:35,131
I like Oda-kun of the basketball team…

26
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,760
Yo, Hanamichi!

27
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:42,597
Cheer up! What's so great
about the basketball team anyway?

28
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:47,852
Bad move, Ohkusu.

29
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:50,146
The word basketball is
strictly off-limits.

30
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,065
{\an8}HEISEI MANUFACTURER BISCUIT

31
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:55,985
{\an8}Hey, should you be snacking
on biscuits during break?

32
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,112
<i>Basket…</i>

33
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:06,454
You should watch your diet more.

34
00:04:06,537 --> 00:04:08,831
<i>You should play basketball more?</i>

35
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:16,339
Last night I saw the movie
<i>The Thief of Baghdad,</i> and…

36
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:18,258
<i>The Thief of Basketball?</i>

37
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:26,140
<i>What’s so great</i>
<i>about Oda-kun of the basketball team…</i>

38
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:28,726
<i>Probably some dumb jock…</i>

39
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,604
<i>I friggin' hate the basketball team!</i>

40
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:34,274
<i>All the world's in spring</i>

41
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,693
<i>while my heart's still in winter…</i>

42
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,446
Excuse me…

43
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,323
Do you like basketball?

44
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:44,993
What?

45
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,122
Do you like basketball?

46
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,584
Just my type…

47
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,588
You're so tall!

48
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:59,674
I wonder who'd be taller,
you or Rukawa-kun?

49
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:02,093
Rukawa? Who's that?

50
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:03,177
-Dunno.
-Dunno.

51
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:06,639
Wow, amazing muscles!

52
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:09,767
Your legs, too…
You're pretty athletic, aren't you?

53
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,269
N… not really…

54
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,481
My name's Haruko Akagi.

55
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:17,275
Do you like basketball?

56
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:20,570
I love it. After all, I'm an athlete!

57
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:23,072
He's recovered!

58
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:28,703
My spring has come!
My spring has finally arrived!

59
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:31,080
There’s hope yet
for your high school life!

60
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:33,082
Quit it, you're making me blush!

61
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:37,170
I will become an athlete!

62
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:48,681
One-two! One-two! One-two!

63
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:55,688
Hey! Hanamichi!

64
00:05:58,232 --> 00:06:00,026
This is the third-year wing!

65
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:04,155
How about these first-year scrubs, huh?

66
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,741
Oh yeah, what a bunch of punks.

67
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:07,992
Want to rough them up?

68
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:14,123
-Stop!
-Stop!

69
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,750
Sit-ups!

70
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:19,045
-Stop it! It’s appalling!
-Don’t do it in the hallway!

71
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,756
The new kids are so full of energy.

72
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:26,511
Athletic guys are so cool!

73
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:30,223
Forget it, let's go.

74
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,726
Hey, you. Redhead.

75
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:36,604
You a first year? What's your name?

76
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:40,108
I'm Sakuragi the athlete.
Nice to meet you!

77
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:45,321
Hey, come to the rooftop after class.

78
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,075
Don't wuss out.

79
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:51,828
Hey!

80
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:57,750
You knocked the wind out of me.
What's the big idea?

81
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:00,878
What's your problem!
You want some of this?

82
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:04,423
I'll knock the wind out of you, too!

83
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:11,305
Cut it out!
Where do you think you are, huh?

84
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:13,182
The third-year wing.

85
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:14,934
Exactly!

86
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:19,355
Let go. That's enough!
Are you trying to kill him?

87
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,565
Hey! Someone, help!

88
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:23,568
-Looks like trouble.
-Shouldn't we call a teacher?

89
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:27,071
Sakuragi-kun!

90
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:32,160
Haruko-san!

91
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:35,246
What are you doing here?

92
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:37,165
Is that third-year student
someone you know?

93
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:40,543
Just a friend. What about you, Haruko-san?

94
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:43,963
I'm here to deliver
my big brother's lunch, but…

95
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:46,966
It makes me nervous coming
to the third-year wing…

96
00:07:47,049 --> 00:07:49,635
Ah, yeah? Me too…

97
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,554
Like hell!

98
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,764
<i>Big brother, huh…</i>

99
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:56,434
Ah? Where are you going, Sakuragi-kun?

100
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:57,560
{\an8}YEAR 3, CLASS 6

101
00:07:57,643 --> 00:07:59,437
{\an8}I thought I'd stop by
and introduce myself…

102
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:02,857
D… don't! Sibling stuff is embarrassing…

103
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,234
Let’s just get back to our classroom.

104
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,444
You think so?

105
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:12,033
-That was amazing.
-Kinda stupid, though.

106
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:12,992
That was scary…

107
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:16,120
Did something happen?

108
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,038
Nori-chan!

109
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,508
Letting yourselves get slapped around
by some first-year punk!

110
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:31,302
Sakuragi, the redhead, huh…

111
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:35,223
As I recall, he was
from Wakou Middle School. So he came here…

112
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:38,267
He’ll always be a middle-schooler to me.

113
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,773
This is where
the basketball team practices.

114
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:52,532
Oh, hey.

115
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:02,166
Back in middle school,
if I left the ball out like this…

116
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,252
I'd get totally chewed out.

117
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:07,505
Ah, I was on the basketball team
in middle school.

118
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,298
Incredible…

119
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:15,721
Now, cut into Haruko Akagi! Layup shot!

120
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,647
You do it, Sakuragi-kun!

121
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,695
To be honest, I'm a bit clumsy.

122
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:33,698
I won’t be playing any basketball here.

123
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:36,617
But I love to watch it!

124
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:39,453
I've watched my big brother play
since I was a kid!

125
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:42,456
Sakuragi-kun, do you know what a dunk is?

126
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,458
Yeah!

127
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:47,128
CREAK CREAK CREAK

128
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:48,462
That's a tank.

129
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:52,550
That's a spike.

130
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:56,887
No, a dunk is the best part of basketball!

131
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:06,981
It's the most exciting play
that gets the crowd going!

132
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:09,483
When it looks like
the backboard’s about to shatter

133
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:12,820
as you stuff the ball through it,
that’s called a slam dunk!

134
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:21,329
{\an8}In middle school, when big brother
dunked, both sides went wild…

135
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:24,582
{\an8}The whole gym would go nuts.
It was amazing!

136
00:10:24,665 --> 00:10:25,541
{\an8}RUN! JUMP!

137
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,169
Rukawa-kun's dunks were pretty great, too…

138
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,171
Rukawa?

139
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:37,053
Whoa! Sakuragi-kun,
you can hold the ball? Awesome!

140
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:42,433
Bah, I'm an athlete.
Nothing to it! Check this out!

141
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:46,145
Amazing! Say, Sakuragi-kun, can you dunk?

142
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:49,023
You're so tall, so you must be able
to jump really high!

143
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:51,859
W… well, I am an athlete…

144
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:55,112
Come on, try it!

145
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:01,369
Slam the ball
right through this hoop, Sakuragi-kun!

146
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:02,953
Jump as high as you can!

147
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:06,874
Wow, my heart's totally pounding now!

148
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,130
<i>Haruko-san really loves basketball, huh…</i>

149
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:14,340
<i>She's cute.</i>

150
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:18,386
<i>Slam dunk, huh… Gotta do it seriously!</i>

151
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:20,596
Here goes, Haruko-san!

152
00:11:20,679 --> 00:11:21,889
All right, do your best!

153
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:25,559
All right!

154
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:31,023
<i>He's running while holding the ball!</i>

155
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,696
Here goes! Slam dunk!

156
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:42,952
W… wow!

157
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:44,995
<i>Slam it right through the hoop!</i>

158
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:48,833
Oh… oh!

159
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:00,803
Awesome, Sakuragi-kun!

160
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:03,222
You missed,
but your jumping ability is amazing!

161
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:07,101
You totally have to join
the basketball team!

162
00:12:07,184 --> 00:12:08,394
Is… that so…

163
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:12,815
Yes, totally! That is so, so amazing!

164
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,734
<i>He's a savior! A savior, big brother!</i>

165
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:18,696
<i>Sakuragi-kun will save</i>
<i>the basketball team!</i>

166
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:35,254
That guy's huge…
as tall as Hanamichi, maybe?

167
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:38,132
Is he a first-year student like us?

168
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:48,142
Well, he rubs me the wrong way.

169
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:51,979
Ow!

170
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:53,230
Be gentle.

171
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:57,735
Sakuragi-kun, how's your head injury?

172
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,945
Haruko-san! I'm all better now!

173
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:03,782
Haruko-chan,
worry more about the backboard.

174
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,951
This guy's head is like a rock.

175
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:10,080
Sakuragi-kun, I turned in
your application for the basketball team.

176
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:13,918
My big brother says you won't get in
unless you have guts, but…

177
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,961
You’ll do just fine. Right, Sakuragi-kun?

178
00:13:16,712 --> 00:13:18,964
I have guts. I'll be all right!

179
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:21,133
{\an8}All right, good luck!

180
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:25,054
Haruko-san's so darn cute!

181
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:28,974
If I could walk with her
to school, I could die happy!

182
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:32,895
Haruko, you’re so brave.

183
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:35,940
You talk with such scary guys so easily!

184
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:38,692
Are you talking about Sakuragi-kun?

185
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:42,112
Yeah. I heard
from the Wakou Middle School guys…

186
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,114
Especially that red-haired guy.

187
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:49,078
He was notorious
for being really bad in middle school.

188
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,830
Haruko, you don't get scared
at all, do you?

189
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:55,042
But Sakuragi-kun's so easy to talk to.

190
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:58,796
I've never felt so relaxed
when talking to someone.

191
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,548
I think he's a good person.

192
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,510
Ah, it's truly spring…

193
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:06,095
This is happiness.

194
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:07,888
Hey, Hanamichi.

195
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:11,767
You’ve been through this before.
Get your hopes up now

196
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:13,769
and the shock will just be worse later

197
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:15,145
when you get shot down.

198
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:21,360
Haruko-chan's certainly cute.
Has a nice personality, too.

199
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,863
Yep, it's true!

200
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:27,408
You think a girl like that
doesn't have a guy?

201
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:29,410
Guys can't leave girls like that alone.

202
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:32,705
-Yup, yup.
-Yup, yup.

203
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:34,164
She's gotta have a guy!

204
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:36,125
What's your problem, guys?

205
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:40,421
-Rukawa must be her boyfriend.
-That Rukawa guy…

206
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:41,881
R… Rukawa?

207
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,758
You’re so tall!

208
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:46,927
I wonder who'd be taller,
you or Rukawa-kun?

209
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:50,431
Rukawa-kun's dunks were pretty great, too…

210
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,934
-Rukawa…
-Yup, yup.

211
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:57,229
Die, Rukawa!

212
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,941
It's not like it's been confirmed yet.

213
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,068
Just ask Haruko-chan directly.

214
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:07,531
Eh? Rukawa-kun? What… what about him?

215
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:11,660
Well, I was wondering
if he was your boyfriend…

216
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:13,829
Look at that nervous response…

217
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:16,165
I guess Rukawa might be her boyfriend…

218
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:19,168
Totally! There's no mistake about it!

219
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:22,171
I guess Rukawa-kun
is your boyfriend, then?

220
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:27,176
No, not at all!
Rukawa-kun doesn't even know me!

221
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,678
W… what?

222
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:32,806
<i>See that? Who's her boyfriend, you idiots!</i>

223
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:35,517
C'mon, pay up, I win.

224
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,145
<i>They were betting on it!</i>

225
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,521
Rukawa-kun is, well…

226
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,981
Yes?

227
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:43,192
He was on the Tomigaoka basketball team.

228
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:48,072
I went to Yonchu.
We had a lot of practice games.

229
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:51,492
<i>The Yonchu team would always</i>
<i>single Rukawa-kun out…</i>

230
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:54,411
<i>But they couldn’t hold him back,</i>
<i>and they kept losing.</i>

231
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:59,166
{\an8}<i>He had three guys constantly on him.</i>

232
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,377
One against three?

233
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:04,463
Basketball teams have five people, so…

234
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:10,386
to get three on one, you have to use two
to deal with the other four guys.

235
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:12,262
Let's see… I get it…

236
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:14,098
{\an8}YONCHU

237
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:19,269
So three guys all tried
to stop him. Tried to, but…

238
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:29,697
<i>Rukawa-kun landed four dunks</i>
<i>past three guards in that game</i>

239
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,741
<i>and totally wiped out Yonchu!</i>

240
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:36,954
<i>He scored 51 points</i>
<i>just by himself in that game.</i>

241
00:16:42,626 --> 00:16:44,920
The image of Rukawa-kun from that day…

242
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:46,463
is stuck in my head even now…

243
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:53,470
Ah, how could I keep talking like this…

244
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:57,266
Sakuragi-kun, you make things
just sort of slip out…

245
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,476
<i>Don't tell me…</i>

246
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:03,063
So, your feelings for Rukawa-kun are…

247
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,273
Just one-sided.

248
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:06,942
Shock!

249
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,569
Shock!

250
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:11,905
I haven't told anyone else about this!

251
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:15,075
You can't tell anybody,
all right, Sakuragi-kun?

252
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:18,037
Ah? Sakuragi-kun?

253
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:22,791
In commemoration
of your high school first!

254
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:25,794
Congratulations, Hanamichi!
It’s the start of a new streak!

255
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,923
Uh-oh, here it comes…

256
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,351
That's not his usual reaction…

257
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:47,357
Shh, it's that song again.

258
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:06,251
This is too sad! Hanamichi!

259
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:09,046
He was really serious this time…

260
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:14,718
Hanamichi!

261
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:18,013
That felt refreshing… ah!

262
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:20,808
YEAR 1, CLASS 7

263
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,352
Is Sakuragi here?

264
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:25,104
Who are you guys?

265
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:27,189
No worries, we'll be gone soon.

266
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,694
Sakuragi! You know what we want, right?

267
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:36,281
Come to the rooftop after class.
Don't wuss out.

268
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:40,911
What the hell…

269
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:43,163
You calling me a wuss?

270
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,748
Uh-oh, he's snapped!

271
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:48,252
Okay, guys, we get the point,
so get out already!

272
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:52,464
Who do you think
you’re talking to? I’ll crush you!

273
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:55,050
Small fry should get lost.

274
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,261
I'm talking to you, Hotta-senpai.

275
00:18:57,344 --> 00:19:01,181
What? Who are you calling
small fry, buddy?

276
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:03,142
Yohei Mito, right?

277
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:05,185
This year's first years
are an energetic bunch.

278
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,563
You bastards!

279
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:11,567
Hey, everyone!
Drop it, or you're all suspended!

280
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:12,484
Hey, Sakuragi!

281
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:18,073
Fine. Mito, you bring the idiot.
We'll take you both on together.

282
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:23,078
Better keep your headcount high,
with so many weaklings.

283
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:28,167
The idiot? You'd better not
be talking about me, huh?

284
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:31,753
Hey, don't run! Hey!

285
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,271
Who's this?

286
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:52,649
Hey, punk. No napping here, get lost!

287
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:55,277
That hurt…

288
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,321
Come on. Turn around and get lost, punk!

289
00:19:57,988 --> 00:20:00,240
Get your rear in gear!

290
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,828
You're a tall one…

291
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,623
You're the one that kicked me?

292
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:11,668
What the hell are you doing?

293
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:17,549
Year 1, Class 10. The name's Kaede Rukawa.

294
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:20,677
No matter how many there are,
I don’t like being woken up.

295
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:28,018
<i>In Hanamichi Sakuragi's high school life…</i>

296
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:30,187
<i>a lone ray of hope finally shone through.</i>

297
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:33,482
<i>But in front of that light stood one man…</i>

298
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,208
<i>You hate me?</i>

299
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:19,046
<i>Haruka-san, that’s a misunderstanding.</i>

300
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:22,716
<i>My life in high school is all messed up,</i>

301
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:25,385
<i>all because of Rukawa.</i>

302
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:27,929
<i>I hate basketball.</i>

303
00:22:28,638 --> 00:22:33,602
<i>Slam Dunk. "Go to hell, basketball!</i>
<i>Hanamichi vs. Rukawa."</i>

304
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:35,187
{\an8}<i>You’ll watch, won’t you?!</i>
